WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:13.270
Tursunay Ziyawudun is part

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.690
of the Turkic ethnic group
known as the Uyghurs,

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.470
Chinese Muslims who mostly live

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.970
in the northwest province of Xinjiang.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.870
There are about 12.8 million
Uyghurs who live there,

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.780
and human rights groups say
that many have become victims

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:30.790
of crimes against humanity at
the hands of the government.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.790
China is accused of imprisoning
over one million Uyghurs

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.130
in re-education camps, sexual abuse,

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.590
and even forced sterilization.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.180
Ziyawudun says she spent 11 months in jail

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.190
for no stated reason.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.523
She was sexually assaulted and tortured.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.040
Communist Party officials have
attributed their treatment

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.240
of the Uyghurs to the war on terror.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.030
In 2008, the region suffered
multiple terrorist attacks

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.560
linked to the East Turkestan
independence movement,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.970
which is a faction within
the Uyghur community

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.980
that wants Xinjiang to separate from China

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.010
and form its own state.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.780
But human rights advocates
say that terrorism

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.540
is just an excuse.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.310
The Chinese have oppressed the Uyghurs

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.530
as part of their push
for radical conformity.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.770
The government describes
the camps as focused

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:35.600
on re-education and career training.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.650
In 2017, when the crackdown intensified,

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.500
Uyghurs were targeted
for wearing head scarfs,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.740
for abstaining from drinking alcohol,

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.350
and for displaying abnormal behaviors,

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.522
like purchasing dumbbells.

00:02:34.608 --> 00:02:37.320
Some attribute the Chinese
government push for conformity

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.220
to capitalism, and Beijing's
desire to staff factories,

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.860
increase production, and surpass
the US on the global stage.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.010
But the Chinese Communist
Party says its goal

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.780
is to build a modern socialist country.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.903
And that description is more apt.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.370
China seeks to impose one identity,

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:02.370
culture, and language on all
of its 1.37 billion people,

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.100
erasing that which does not conform.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.670
From the policies of Mao,

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.510
to those of Lenin and Stalin,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.710
when command and control of
society is imposed uniformity,

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:16.690
it inevitably leads to
human rights violations.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.350
Ziyawudun says that she felt

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.300
as if the Chinese government set out

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.550
to eradicate her culture and ethnicity.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.500
The Chinese government has
ever more sophisticated tools

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.230
of surveillance at its disposal.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.640
And it allegedly provides
local authorities

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.790
with lists that detail how
to identify extremists.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.030
In Ziyawudun's case, she
says she was arrested

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.060
when she returned to
Xinjiang from Kazakhstan,

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.780
where she had been living
with her Kazak husband.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.600
Ziyawudun says she was released

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.630
after her husband advocated on her behalf.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.220
She made it to the US under the protection

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.480
of the Uyghur Human Rights Project,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.320
an organization that seeks
to promote the rights

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.280
of the Uyghur and other
Turkic Muslims from Xinjiang.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.210
Today Ziyawudun lives in a suburb of D.C.

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:18.690
She says that her heart
aches for her family

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.080
and the other Uyghurs back home,

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.440
millions of whom are
still being imprisoned,

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:27.380
tortured, and surveilled in
their most private spaces,

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.090
including their living
rooms, dining areas,

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:33.673
and prayer spaces,
according to one report.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.470
Although the US has
condemned the mistreatment

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:48.070
of the Uyghurs, and government officials

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:51.460
are boycotting the Beijing
Olympics in protest,

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.970
we've admitted zero new Uyghur refugees

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.790
in the last two years.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.790
Welcoming foreigners like Ziyawudun

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.770
is what has allowed the US to
avoid becoming a monoculture.

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:04.670
And our diversity of
thought and experience

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.440
is the secret of American capitalism.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.790
China's erasing of the Uyghur culture

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.910
and its decision to surveil, imprison,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.430
and torture the Uyghur people in pursuit

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.847
of becoming the leading global superpower

